2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] How to use it with CGEventSourceKeyState
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] // Call this every frame or on a timer
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] void updateVIC20Keyboard(uint8_t matrix[8]) {
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1]     // Clear matrix first
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1]     memset(matrix, 0, 8);
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1]     CGEventSourceStateID source = kCGEventSourceStateHIDSystemState;
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1]     for (int i = 0; i < VIC20_KEY_COUNT; i++) {
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1]         const KeyMapping *m = &vic20KeyMap[i];
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1]         if (CGEventSourceKeyState(source, m->macCode)) {
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1]             matrix[m->vicRow] |= (1 << m->vicCol);
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1]         }
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1]     }
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] }
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] Notes / Improvements
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] - Shift handling: By also mapping `kVK_Shift` and `kVK_RightShift`, upper case and symbols
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] work naturally.
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] - £ key: `kVK_ANSI_Backslash` is a placeholder. You can change it to whatever key you
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] prefer.
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] - Left arrow (←): Currently mapped to `[`. Change if you want something else.
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] - Commodore key (C=): Mapped to `Option`. You can change to `Command` if you prefer.
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] - Function keys: `F1/F3/F5/F7` are mapped directly. `F2/F4/F6/F8` are usually handled by
2026-08-06 16:38:10 [grok-build-0.1] checking shift + the odd function keys in your emulator logic.
