2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] No, the previous mapping had several inaccuracies for the actual VIC-20 keyboard matrix.
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] Key issues included:
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] - Wrong row for F5 (it belongs in row 7, not mixed in).
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] - Incorrect or missing assignments for the Commodore (C=) key.
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] - Some symbol keys were assigned to the wrong matrix positions (e.g. * , + , = , 0, 2, 4, 6, 8).
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] - The left arrow (←) is at row 1 col 7 (some tables also list it at row 6 col 7, but emulators
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] typically use row 1 col 7 for the physical key).
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] - Row 7 was incomplete and had incorrect keys.
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] - A few Mac key codes were not the most practical matches for the VIC-20 layout.
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] The correct standard VIC-20 8x8 matrix positions (used by emulators like VICE) are:
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] Row 0: DEL, 3, 5, 7, 9, +, £, 1
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] Row 1: RETURN, W, R, Y, I, P, *, ←
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] Row 2: ↓, A, D, G, J, L, ;, CTRL
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] Row 3: F7, Z, C, B, M, ., R SHIFT, STOP
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] Row 4: SPACE, S, F, H, K, :, =, →
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] Row 5: F1, E, T, U, O, @, ↑, Q
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] Row 6: F3, L SHIFT, X, V, N, ,, /, ← (per some tables)
2026-08-06 16:41:48 [grok-build-0.1] Row 7: F5, C=, (mostly unused)
