2026-08-18 19:39:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] Yes, on macOS (in Carbon / CoreGraphics / HIToolbox), `kVK_ANSI_A` is indeed `0x00` (`0`).
2026-08-18 19:39:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 19:39:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] Because of this, using `0` as an empty/unused matrix placeholder creates a conflict where the
2026-08-18 19:39:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] A key is ignored. To avoid this collision, unmapped matrix entries should use a sentinel
2026-08-18 19:39:43 [gemini-3.7-flash] value like `-1` (or `0xFFFF`).
