2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.007 23.14KB 6.53s
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] Yes, both `0x30` and `0x1E` are valid, official NMOS 6502 opcodes.
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] Opcode `$30` (decimal 48)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Instruction: `BMI` (Branch on Result Minus / Negative)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Addressing Mode: Relative
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Byte Length: 2 bytes (`30 nn`)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Cycles:
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * 2 cycles (branch not taken)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * 3 cycles (branch taken, same page)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash]   * 4 cycles (branch taken across page boundary)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Operation: Branches to `PC + offset` if the Negative flag (N) is set (`1`).
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] Opcode `$1E` (decimal 30)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Instruction: `ASL` (Arithmetic Shift Left)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Addressing Mode: Absolute, X-indexed (`$aaaa,X`)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Byte Length: 3 bytes (`1E LL HH`)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Cycles: 7 cycles (always takes 7 cycles, even without a page boundary cross, as it is a
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] read-modify-write instruction)
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Operation: Shifts the contents of memory address `(HHLL + X)` left by 1 bit. Bit 7 goes
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] into the Carry flag (C), and bit 0 becomes `0`. Sets the N and Z flags based on the result.
2026-08-18 20:38:49 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
