2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.008 27.90KB 4.21s
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] In standard Commodore PET hardware, the 6520 PIA 1 is mapped to the 16-bit address
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] `E810`, not the zero-page/8-bit address `00E8`.
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] There are two primary reasons why row selection fails during the keyboard scan routine (`SCNKEY`):
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. Address Decoding (16-bit vs 8-bit)
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] The PET Kernal accesses the keyboard controller via 16-bit absolute addresses:
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Row Select (Output): Address `$E810` (PIA 1 Port A / `PRA`)
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Column Read (Input): Address `$E812` (PIA 1 Port B / `PRB`)
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] If your emulator checks memory addresses using only a single byte (e.g., `address === 0xE8`), it
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] will intercept wrong writes or miss the full 16-bit address `$E810`.
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. PIA Data Direction Register (DDR) vs. Output Register Selection
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] The 6520 PIA shares the same memory address for both the Data Direction Register (`DDRA`)
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] and the Peripheral Output Register (`PRA`).
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] Which internal register gets updated depends on Bit 2 of the Control Register A
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] (`CRA`) at address `$E811`:
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `CRA` Bit 2 = `0`: Writing to `$E810` modifies the Data Direction Register (`DDRA`).
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] • `CRA` Bit 2 = `1`: Writing to `$E810` modifies Port A outputs (`PRA`), which drives the
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] keyboard row decoder.
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] During system boot, the PET Kernal sets `CRA` bit 2 to `1`. If your emulator does not track this
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] control bit, writes intended for the keyboard decoder might be misrouted.
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] Correct TypeScript Emulator Implementation
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] // Memory Addresses for 6520 PIA 1
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] const PET_PIA1_PRA: number = 0xE810;  // Port A / DDR A
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] const PET_PIA1_CRA: number = 0xE811;  // Control Register A
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] const PET_PIA1_PRB: number = 0xE812;  // Port B / DDR B
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] const PET_PIA1_CRB: number = 0xE813;  // Control Register B
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] let pia1ControlA: number = 0x00;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] let pia1DdrA: number = 0x00;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] let pia1PortA: number = 0x00;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] export function writePetHardware(address: number, value: number): void {
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	if (address === PET_PIA1_CRA) {
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		pia1ControlA = value;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		return;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	}
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	if (address === PET_PIA1_PRA) {
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		// Check Bit 2 of Control Register A
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		const isOutputRegisterSelected: boolean = (pia1ControlA & 0x04) !== 0;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		if (isOutputRegisterSelected) {
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 			// Bits 0..3 drive the 74145 BCD-to-Decimal row decoder
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 			pia1PortA = value & 0x0F;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		} else {
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 			pia1DdrA = value;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		}
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		return;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	}
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] }
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] export function readPetHardware(address: number): number {
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	if (address === PET_PIA1_PRB) {
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		// Read columns (PB0..PB7) for active row (0-9)
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 		return readPetKeyboardMatrix(pia1PortA);
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	}
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 	return 0xFF;
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] }
2026-08-18 21:20:03 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
