2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] The overall multi-system architecture is well-structured and covers a broad range of platforms
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] (Commodore PET/VIC-20/C64/TED, Apple II, Atari DVG, and Ben Eater 6502 breadboard kit).
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] A few key observations and potential considerations across the shared files:
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] 1. `macosffi.ts` — Keyboard Matrix Sentinel Check
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] • In `readPetKeyboard()`, the check `if (key)` will evaluate to `false` for `kVK_ANSI_A` (`0x00`).
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] • If `0` remains the placeholder for unassigned matrix slots, pressing the physical A key
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] will not register. Defining a sentinel constant (e.g., `-1`) for empty matrix cells and checking
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] `if (key >= 0)` avoids this collision.
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] 2. `macosaudio.ts` — AudioQueue Buffer Recycling
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] • In `playAudio()`, new native buffers are allocated via `AudioQueueAllocateBuffer` on every call
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] and held indefinitely in `audioBuffers`.
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] • For long emulation runs, this can lead to memory growth. Utilizing the `noOpCallback` (which is
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] called when macOS completes playback of an enqueued buffer) to reclaim or reuse a fixed ring of
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] buffers (typically 2 to 4 buffers) would provide steady streaming without unbounded allocations.
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] 3. `machine.ts` — PET PIA Hardware Interaction
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] • The PIA 1 Port A write routing in `writePET()` now accounts for `CRA` Bit 2 before passing the
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] row index to `scanKeyboard()`.
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] • Reading `E812` (`PIA1_PB`) properly clears the interrupt flags on `E813` (`CB1`/`CB2`) and
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] queries the active matrix state via `readPetMatrix()`.
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] • The newly integrated opcodes (`1E` for `ASL abs,X` and `5E` for `LSR abs,X`) correctly handle
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] read-modify-write addressing through `targetAbsoluteX`.
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] 
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] If you would like to refine any specific subsystem (such as buffer cycling in AudioQueue, the full
2026-08-18 21:41:12 [gemini-3.7-flash] PET Business/Graphics matrix array, or VIA/CIA timer interrupts), let me know.
